torname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(10x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb82788-efbe-50de-b226-6bde5d6aedf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5eb82788-efbe-50de-b226-6bde5d6aedf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317886} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ffe2b0-f398-575b-afe8-d12d64c3f4fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318580}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ec7ce12f-cbf4-5c03-8053-383589db4d45" :question/math-academy-id "q-346368" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{4},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $2\\pi /3$ | $2\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u))\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)) \\\\  & =4(-1+2) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319363 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9793ffe-67cc-5645-9b00-c140cc88e2aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9793ffe-67cc-5645-9b00-c140cc88e2aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318233} :answer-field/id #uuid "24f68f41-ba58-5d4c-9946-589591e9529a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318497}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8ccae74f-35c6-57d0-a03f-750b899cc692" :question/math-academy-id "q-350060" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}3{sec}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\pi /4$ | $0$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}3{sec}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{0}{sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u){|}_{-\\pi /4}^{0} \\\\  & =3(0-(-1)) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85c49c8e-61d5-5e58-a395-01a4e606b7d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c49c8e-61d5-5e58-a395-01a4e606b7d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318020} :answer-field/id #uuid "773a7395-c2f8-5568-bc4a-ffe056234383" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318675}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d188146f-1019-54e0-bddf-9c317ac884d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-350071" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=x-\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /3$ | $2\\pi /3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-4(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)) \\\\  & =-4(1-2) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde6a22f-af92-5d05-a00e-ee43025b38b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bde6a22f-af92-5d05-a00e-ee43025b38b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429918} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4b1c21c-bb6c-5c53-b4e6-f6635e6c2be4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429928}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66f3c3b9-c1e9-58f7-9604-16a02027760f" :question/math-academy-id "q-355818" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /20}^{\\pi /10}5{csc}^{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=5x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /20$ | $\\pi /10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /4$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /20}^{\\pi /10}5{csc}^{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}5{csc}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)) \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429933 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02192a18-96df-5c9c-86d1-fd39f10cc96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429909} {:answer/id #uuid "258b40a9-d7f7-5e38-ab76-8707b1a1a9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429911} {:answer/id #uuid "59c2d43f-3033-53cf-a498-afe18808b478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429913} {:answer/id #uuid "605c38a6-bd94-5054-abeb-196bc585d8b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429915} {:answer/id #uuid "f513628d-4c08-512b-85ac-0d46df6f115b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02192a18-96df-5c9c-86d1-fd39f10cc96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429909} :answer-field/id #uuid "f070068b-56d2-50d4-88fa-ab05a0ca7204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429929}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a6be6fa7-2d6e-5c8a-ab1e-bb035341f649" :question/math-academy-id "q-10578" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=x-\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /6$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡u{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d53a8c66-6804-52ec-8840-edd3d4929673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d53a8c66-6804-52ec-8840-edd3d4929673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553296} :answer-field/id #uuid "95531b96-24f8-5a49-ac02-3bfee0bf2b70" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "248312e6-be46-5549-b1e3-5f70f146c665" :question/math-academy-id "q-346363" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /8}3{csc}^{2}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=4x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /12$ | $\\pi /8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /8}3{csc}^{2}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}3{csc}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u))\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(0+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "114cd42d-ba52-5869-9448-93a17d0920de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580410} {:answer/id #uuid "4edb41e5-8763-5f56-92a0-923aac665da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580521} {:answer/id #uuid "921a2907-c9c2-55f3-a5c1-c088eea2d222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580634} {:answer/id #uuid "d55a31f3-9f9c-5cf2-9b86-12761d10e402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580719} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7d360d-043f-5158-a0ad-2486d0c89e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4edb41e5-8763-5f56-92a0-923aac665da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580521} :answer-field/id #uuid "1acf62d4-21d8-564e-9008-9e94eb8fcbe4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580805}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d4c2c34-0e64-5420-b51f-0cd0b469fb94" :question/math-academy-id "q-13524" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580890 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d3b08c5-67ec-556a-9db8-346afb23990d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d3b08c5-67ec-556a-9db8-346afb23990d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580406} :answer-field/id #uuid "04e9c3ac-e070-5fba-b495-8a7967767527" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580791}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ccd5c9d-8efc-5890-b6e0-7b6adea1884d" :question/math-academy-id "q-350055" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /12$ | $\\pi /9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /4$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)) \\\\  & =2(2-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =4-2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d020a63-ff8a-5103-950e-32a99925bad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d020a63-ff8a-5103-950e-32a99925bad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580596} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a470524-f944-5b81-ad61-34953fcf821f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580819}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "891837cc-fc66-582c-9fc5-1ebbcc953137" :question/math-academy-id "q-350053" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /9}3{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /18$ | $\\pi /9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /9}3{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}3{sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00684a2f-d8bf-539e-8768-dd9c37ae4462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580384} {:answer/id #uuid "3bb0ba8b-b756-54d7-84d7-fbb88e5ca0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580488} {:answer/id #uuid "6a23ee15-1ca3-55ab-ab89-e68612ea242f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580564} {:answer/id #uuid "6d602fb9-1975-5b9a-b57b-0b866e48bf8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580573} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d0d7d0-b097-58a3-b109-3bdf30daaa49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d602fb9-1975-5b9a-b57b-0b866e48bf8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580573} :answer-field/id #uuid "efe5bc0a-b315-5b23-93da-8951c85ccafd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580875}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93bebf8e-0e85-5d99-abd0-30d0a01cdaa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-113979" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02a0e0ac-e727-5461-b976-19c124b8b464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580388} {:answer/id #uuid "4890fcde-2797-5117-8088-b582d7722617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580508} {:answer/id #uuid "6d616f73-2fa0-5847-8b9f-9a01caad223b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580574} {:answer/id #uuid "cb597cd5-c5ef-508d-a0c1-618aa29883dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580705} {:answer/id #uuid "e36ac8bb-58e1-59ed-a6aa-fe6e8c50369c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb597cd5-c5ef-508d-a0c1-618aa29883dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580705} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6e41e02-7a09-5398-bc9b-a3b506f57d51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580861}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9cfe1a63-f205-5796-abd7-66f03dc0449c" :question/math-academy-id "q-13655" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601948 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2793389a-a6be-59df-bc34-ec2d332ef005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601623} {:answer/id #uuid "9949b34a-44b2-5aab-aa8a-f06da3c9f818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601715} {:answer/id #uuid "d871a8f6-a53a-5d66-bea4-b8ccbd3eb897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601775} {:answer/id #uuid "f362563c-190c-50ef-9666-faada8e9f4b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601798} {:answer/id #uuid "f4655e3f-33f9-5353-81d1-9b2c1670e6a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4655e3f-33f9-5353-81d1-9b2c1670e6a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601801} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b02c2b7-ab80-5b62-9eaa-c0d8af84102c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601852}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5ec3a44-706a-552a-b9fc-e5121c81e87c" :question/math-academy-id "q-10595" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /3$ | $2\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\left(-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186611583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194fd8af-b040-5b37-b284-479fc28e14fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "194fd8af-b040-5b37-b284-479fc28e14fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611112} :answer-field/id #uuid "80cdbf21-5d83-5f11-a83b-a6feecf8976c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611510}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e66bab1-d394-5399-b025-c983e9b8e368" :question/math-academy-id "q-350057" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}6{sec}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /4$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}6{sec}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}6{sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u){|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =3(1-0) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186658965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a62534-23f8-5551-b309-2bfcf1b6c7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50a62534-23f8-5551-b309-2bfcf1b6c7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658519} :answer-field/id #uuid "7782799c-d581-57e2-83cc-457e771d14a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658863}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b022582d-7a73-572b-bcbe-ac8b549acb6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-350061" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=x-\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u){|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6(2-1) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da28418d-ce9f-5f59-b794-596465adadd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da28418d-ce9f-5f59-b794-596465adadd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677441} :answer-field/id #uuid "e97f93d6-8717-5343-9503-137259aa5d19" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677447}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03595741-d485-53cb-871d-b8d426aec985" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{24}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{18}} 2 \\tan{\\left(6 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(6 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=6 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=6.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{24}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{18}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{24}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{18}} 2 \\tan{\\left(6 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(6 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{\\sec{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}=\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "209c646d-cdab-5040-9f0e-4b1c81b98409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "209c646d-cdab-5040-9f0e-4b1c81b98409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677394} :answer-field/id #uuid "d871cdba-45ff-5925-9b05-a112885553d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677440}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "073aeb1d-5ede-5b0d-bfc8-d37ff2d691c4" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int - 3 \\sec^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int - 3 \\sec^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{3 \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{3 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "befba929-9fda-5f48-afb7-dc9545acb297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 5 \\sqrt{2} + \\frac{10 \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "befba929-9fda-5f48-afb7-dc9545acb297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 5 \\sqrt{2} + \\frac{10 \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677433} :answer-field/id #uuid "7831f77e-feb9-5909-9370-a77527b7e4ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677416}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c351c96-eb00-5911-ae50-4a666f600e22" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} - \\frac{5 \\tan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\sec{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\\\x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} - \\frac{5 \\tan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\sec{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-5\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[- 5 \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}=\\left(- 5 \\sqrt{2}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{10 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n- 5 \\sqrt{2} + \\frac{10 \\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fef5887b-26b3-5aa8-9e51-1e7c0d919e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2 + 2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fef5887b-26b3-5aa8-9e51-1e7c0d919e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2 + 2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677457} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8eaa502-7fe5-5d6a-a807-4483e127b7ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677445}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1dd0d444-b9a6-56a7-81ab-1f737d2a3c8a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{0} 6 \\tan{\\left(- 3 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(- 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{\\pi}{12}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed bounds decrease; keep their order when subtracting endpoint values.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{0} 6 \\tan{\\left(- 3 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(- 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-2\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0} \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[- 2 \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0}=\\left(-2\\right)-\\left(- 2 \\sqrt{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n-2 + 2 \\sqrt{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6896d6f-761d-578c-81d5-360fcd6adfd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7 \\cot{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6896d6f-761d-578c-81d5-360fcd6adfd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7 \\cot{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677444} :answer-field/id #uuid "a07e1c67-4ecb-5837-8958-50a04cdd0b19" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677427}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ce29796-c18d-5902-a450-5c6a1b1b5220" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 7 \\csc^{2}{\\left(5 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=5 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 7 \\csc^{2}{\\left(5 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{7}{5}\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{5}\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{7 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}}{5}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{7 \\cot{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{5}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e97b264a-92e7-5a52-b1a2-2a700eb0283c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{2}}{2} + 3 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e97b264a-92e7-5a52-b1a2-2a700eb0283c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{2}}{2} + 3 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677446} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a5e5342-0591-5102-b507-47697fd55990" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677411}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "36cd3b27-f6e8-592d-99e4-5ee5368b313f" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}} - \\frac{3 \\cot{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}} - \\frac{3 \\cot{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{9}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{9 \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}=\\left(3 \\sqrt{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{9 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{2}}{2} + 3 \\sqrt{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6e3a9b4-6967-5e80-a68f-df56357b77da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7 \\csc{\\left(5 x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6e3a9b4-6967-5e80-a68f-df56357b77da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7 \\csc{\\left(5 x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677452} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa22f9a-1118-50d0-810b-11c451d6a55d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677442}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39226942-711b-55fb-b672-0b9498c72c21" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int - 7 \\cot{\\left(5 x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(5 x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=5 x + \\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int - 7 \\cot{\\left(5 x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(5 x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{7}{5}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{7}{5}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{7 \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{5}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7 \\csc{\\left(5 x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}}{5}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "987b7251-5c21-5376-8e01-a0bfd0d15fad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cot{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "987b7251-5c21-5376-8e01-a0bfd0d15fad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cot{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677424} :answer-field/id #uuid "3081ec4b-ef17-50e3-b5cc-7ce15a85ee9e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677397}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ef6f8f6-1922-5bdc-a2f1-cc3e307583e8" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n-\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\cot{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\cot{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f99cafe-bcac-5579-8d6d-6c31fd9aa27d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f99cafe-bcac-5579-8d6d-6c31fd9aa27d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677412} :answer-field/id #uuid "999f1e33-f8f3-597c-94a5-235188d9ae11" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677425}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55663b8c-42f7-596d-83e8-240de0ec9b1d" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{10}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{15}} - 4 \\cot{\\left(- 5 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- 5 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 5 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-5.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{\\pi}{10}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=- \\frac{\\pi}{15}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed bounds decrease; keep their order when subtracting endpoint values.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{10}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{15}} - 4 \\cot{\\left(- 5 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- 5 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{4}{5}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{4 \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{5}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}=\\left(- \\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{15}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{4}{5}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{15}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a633cb9-c226-54ca-aa17-c258b57d502e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a633cb9-c226-54ca-aa17-c258b57d502e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677400} :answer-field/id #uuid "4411b9bd-2f0d-5663-9506-5db3b279da70" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677404}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5915e3a9-56f6-54b6-939f-1f29ec463eca" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{0} \\frac{2 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{\\pi}{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\\\x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed bounds decrease; keep their order when subtracting endpoint values.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{0} \\frac{2 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{4 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}=\\left(\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{9}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{9}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec8055a-0770-5844-aceb-1096e8a3b4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 - \\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec8055a-0770-5844-aceb-1096e8a3b4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 - \\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677402} :answer-field/id #uuid "f28432f9-fdb3-57cf-97ac-acfd970c0f72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677451}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "619d9def-2035-560b-b2fc-426e1f28c7bd" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{7 \\pi}{4}}^{- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\frac{5 \\tan{\\left(- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\sec{\\left(- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{7 \\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\\\x=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed bounds decrease; keep their order when subtracting endpoint values.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{7 \\pi}{4}}^{- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\frac{5 \\tan{\\left(- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\sec{\\left(- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{15}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{15 \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}=\\left(- \\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\left(-15\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n15 - \\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c145488d-7ae1-56c1-a8eb-8c26014398ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\tan{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c145488d-7ae1-56c1-a8eb-8c26014398ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\tan{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677435} :answer-field/id #uuid "43695357-3206-5da3-8964-0cbc3811fe60" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677403}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69e31cbe-7694-52bc-a3ff-a9360a8fffab" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{\\tan{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{\\tan{\\left(- 2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "faceb4f1-8802-5949-89b6-ff9589308076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{9} - \\frac{10 \\sqrt{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "faceb4f1-8802-5949-89b6-ff9589308076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{9} - \\frac{10 \\sqrt{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677455} :answer-field/id #uuid "c58627f9-6c8a-5834-9ee8-34cfc235dbac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677437}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7176dd16-0df4-55a7-aeeb-1801ac33a090" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{18}} \\frac{5 \\cot{\\left(- \\frac{3 x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- \\frac{3 x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- \\frac{3 x}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{18}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed bounds decrease; keep their order when subtracting endpoint values.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{18}} \\frac{