2894a9-0e0a-5435-b00c-654abc55aab0" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678139}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "262ce555-2ea1-5af2-90b8-7a5c412925cb" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 4 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sec{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\sec{\\left(0 \\right)}=1,\\quad \\sec{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right)}=2$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 4 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[2 \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}=\\left(4\\right)-\\left(2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e4d7c72-6826-51f9-851a-030b3f004aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e4d7c72-6826-51f9-851a-030b3f004aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678189} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7af3103-1064-53cb-a423-c5073d533749" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678196}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "399b103b-f9fc-5fcb-9095-9fb0189a1c1d" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 3 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sec{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{3 \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dffc9365-6a7a-5e28-b7de-12da0e7f08b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dffc9365-6a7a-5e28-b7de-12da0e7f08b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678225} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a5872b9-abe8-5166-9675-198f966ed97f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678149}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3b7aac27-412c-5a90-a059-92216a7c258c" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} 2 \\sec^{2}{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\tan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\tan{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}=1,\\quad \\tan{\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}=-1$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} 2 \\sec^{2}{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}=\\left(1\\right)-\\left(-1\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56c65302-d79a-5cb1-aade-bbb618c33fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\csc{\\left(2 x + 3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56c65302-d79a-5cb1-aade-bbb618c33fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\csc{\\left(2 x + 3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678158} :answer-field/id #uuid "703b45b6-fdc2-56d4-b0f7-af144b3f364c" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678165}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c987452-833d-52ca-801c-e7c865c4a892" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\cot{\\left(2 x + 3 \\right)} \\csc{\\left(2 x + 3 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "