17592186678212} {:answer/id #uuid "cf85c922-e65b-5d41-9423-8046a0fd0955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678218} {:answer/id #uuid "dda4e21f-2ec7-54f7-a1a4-5560a9a83061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678223} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5cd4ce-db03-5b32-ad63-0cdfc999aec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678230} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8a1f8b-973c-5fd3-99b4-6f2281ccbac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec5cd4ce-db03-5b32-ad63-0cdfc999aec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678230} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7e38452-080f-5305-9fc3-ce6011996a71" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678234}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86df9637-597a-5564-98ec-e1285a2b614d" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=4 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e47027d5-cebb-5a6e-ba2a-199f22a1dfcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e47027d5-cebb-5a6e-ba2a-199f22a1dfcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678226} :answer-field/id #uuid "726fbe57-9e99-5ca8-a32c-2927b6ccd612" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678167}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a12513cf-5b77-57ed-9d9c-cdf66ea9782e" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} 4 \\cot{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\csc{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}=2,\\quad \\csc{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=1$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{12}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} 4 \\cot{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- 2 \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}=\\left(-2\\right)-\\left(-4\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2bc3098-5bc7-5aa1-b282-dbb062bc1a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2bc3098-5bc7-5aa1-b282-dbb062bc1a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678220} :answer-field/id #uuid "80ad7916-a685-5554-9389-9c7d724f927f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678177}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a22f82c7-fd5e-5819-8731-d3a4255f5f8f" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 4 \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\tan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x + 3$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\tan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\tan{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678192 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a762ae91-08c8-5dc1-ab3e-8b0ec39af452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a762ae91-08c8-5dc1-ab3e-8b0ec39af452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678195} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5559ef8-9e0d-51c7-9165-14b66785793b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3775cc7-4ca1-5792-8e8e-67e74410350a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{8}}^{0} 4 \\sec^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\tan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\tan{\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}=-1,\\quad \\tan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{\\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{8}}^{0} 4 \\sec^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0} \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[2 \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0}=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(-2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce2d1382-34fd-5922-985d-48032fb59127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce2d1382-34fd-5922-985d-48032fb59127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678215} :answer-field/id #uuid "768c7847-4f5d-58f7-8535-737636a3cad4" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678169}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b03573b5-3c33-54e5-ba16-b877200034cd" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} 4 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\cot{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=0,\\quad \\cot{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}=1$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} 4 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-2\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[2 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}=\\left(2\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9e6cfa2-30b7-57fc-bf92-13ef834aa870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9e6cfa2-30b7-57fc-bf92-13ef834aa870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678229} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec68e414-0ec0-5fdf-9da0-e316467f9a94" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678231}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c697346a-a2b5-5ea9-944d-83b5b405b4f7" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} 3 \\csc^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\cot{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}=1,\\quad \\cot{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=0$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} 3 \\csc^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{3 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b076dd84-df83-5834-9e95-dc75f15ca11d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\tan{\\left(3 - 3 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b076dd84-df83-5834-9e95-dc75f15ca11d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\tan{\\left(3 - 3 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678202} :answer-field/id #uuid "71ab5c94-fed8-57da-b4b1-38d582c32381" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678166}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cd8e3e77-0528-50e5-85fc-4e26a37d7199" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 3 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 - 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\tan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3 - 3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 - 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-\\left(\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n-\\left(\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\tan{\\left(3 - 3 x \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee6c3df-237e-5e70-9f15-cec8532a2c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678137} {:answer/id #uuid "29c28d4f-6e45-589c-897c-de611c89158a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678143} {:answer/id #uuid "90da945a-f6e0-59f6-92b3-d12ce86dc388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678184} {:answer/id #uuid "95070805-8217-526a-b651-45362a73710e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678185} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6c093f-6262-50ab-8d93-9e07c190ca43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95070805-8217-526a-b651-45362a73710e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678185} :answer-field/id #uuid "50233114-8bfc-5a3a-babb-48379d4ea1b4" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678155}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf52a268-c2f4-5263-9f3b-a89d482dc6d7" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=3 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{\\left(3 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\tan{\\left(3 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e81b010-490c-570b-93d2-e5a808604b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678154} {:answer/id #uuid "66926c42-3b79-5096-85a7-54ab5f3f57d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678164} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2aefb5-09af-5327-a2db-3e09ad104fd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678173} {:answer/id #uuid "818a4297-b6ce-53d2-ac25-b2db9ddd9960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678178} {:answer/id #uuid "b74ab3a2-4948-5b2f-b5c5-4353b4c86973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e81b010-490c-570b-93d2-e5a808604b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678154} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b1f161-876f-5583-b647-1bb23875ff37" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678209}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf61ea9c-58bc-510f-ad29-02ae8d17f5da" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=4 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int \\cot{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\cot{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b52b8be3-1572-53a3-a178-6a3cfe9a9008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b52b8be3-1572-53a3-a178-6a3cfe9a9008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678203} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9be053-8ff7-5a09-8987-120e07c9f6ee" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678183}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0a9d12a-1c6a-5869-82ed-3b368443b0d4" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 2 \\tan{\\left(- 2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(- 2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sec{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\sec{\\left(0 \\right)}=1,\\quad \\sec{\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right)}=2$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 2 \\tan{\\left(- 2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(- 2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-\\left(\\int_{0}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{3}}=\\left(-2\\right)-\\left(-1\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n-1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e4f9c28-3e7f-5518-a969-379c6d383efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678174} {:answer/id #uuid "9633ff6f-dd3a-5f0d-a2d8-42b70911a8df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}