nswer/id #uuid "fa1ec0d5-0a6f-5861-8adf-094ce7847be3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678235} :answer-field/id #uuid "85edd87a-47ba-5b47-b967-0cd7189874fc" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678181}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe829f07-c75c-52fb-a210-8165808e94ed" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cot{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\csc{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=1,\\quad \\csc{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}=2$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cot{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{\\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}=\\left(1\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions With Linear Arguments"}]}
